## same diff with the LFN suffix (everything after 'HH:MM ') stripped on both sides
$ diff mdir-ci-nolfn.txt kernel-nolfn.txt && echo IDENTICAL
IDENTICAL with LFN suffixes stripped on both sides (20 lines)

The only remaining difference is the LFN suffixes. That CI run's mdir printed none (except
'2026 january notes', whose short-name checksum is 0) because the corpus stored the LFN
checksum in the wrong byte, fixed in 4b1ebb2. Whether real mdir now prints each suffix,
including UPPER.TXT whose LFN equals its short name, is UNVERIFIED until the next CI stage 9.
